 "text": "Hello, how's your day been so far? You need good solid platform to start on, like rock or large boulder. Then use fire starter steel to dig a small pit in the dampest wood, and light it before you leave it. Yes, they're great for starting a fire in poor conditions. Holding one in each hand and spinning while you switch is the key. Put the sweetest one right at the top where it's freshest, and work down. A small cup hewn across a few branches will do. Use a teapot and fill it at the sink before you leave, or pour it into your mug as you pass the kitchen. Knock it over onto all sides, then turn it a few hours before you go to bed. That way it' fully cold in the morning.",
